{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>To dwell there, saying.</b> Its saying <b>leimor</b> alludes to what the Sages of blessed memory said (Ketubot 110b) that there is a mitzvah to dwell in the land of Canaan, and this is its saying <b>to dwell there, leimor</b> — as though it said leimor, to dwell there." "<b>Further</b>, it may be explained by examining the verse's saying <b>יָצְאוּ אֲנָשִׁים בְּנֵי בְלִיַּעַל</b>: why did it say ״אֲנָשִׁים״ — it would have been sufficient to say ״בְּנֵי בְלִיַּעַל״ and I know that they are men, and if it means to say men and not minors — this does not need a verse to exclude them, for anyone who has not reached the age of punishment does not need to be excluded. Rather, the verse intends to say that although it says ״יָצְאוּ אֲנָשִׁים״, meaning that they are righteous, as they of blessed memory said (Numbers Rabbah 16) — ״אֲנָשִׁים״ in Scripture means righteous men — therefore its saying <b>leimor, יָצְאוּ אֲנָשִׁים</b>, the verse informs you that you must treat them as wicked men and remove from them the presumption of fitness." "<b>Further</b>, it intends that even if you did not hear the matter clearly — that the seducers went out — but rather a report from which it could be understood that they went out, etc., <b>וְדָרַשְׁתָּ</b> etc. — meaning, he shall make an investigation and inquiry to determine whether there is substance to the rumor heard. And this is its saying <b>וְדָרַשְׁתָּ וְחָקַרְתָּ וְשָׁאַלְתָּ</b>; and it would have been proper to put ״וְשָׁאַלְתָּ״ first, since it is the questioning, and afterward the investigation and inquiry. Rather, it intends to say that he should investigate the initial report he heard to see whether there are witnesses to the matter, and only afterward question the witnesses' testimony to judge on the basis of their testimony."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:17:21.485784671Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}